  "decision": "Keep ownership transfer: it removes 20,001 execution-thread allocations and about 1.36 MB allocation traffic per 20,000-file walk in both stat modes, with unchanged execution peak and result parity. macOS timings crossed cache regimes; pinned Linux 50-walk medians moved -0.5% with stat and +1.2% without stat, so no throughput claim is supported. This does not validate lazy record fields: stat:false skips metadata reads and changes error timing, and a new record representation would need equivalent behavior evidence."
